---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base>
  <section class="section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy matters.</h1>
    <p class="lead">This is a public competition preview of ITKeepers V2, not the official ITKeepers production launch. This notice covers inquiries sent through the preview's contact and free IT consultation forms.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section light">
    <h2>Information you submit</h2>
    <p>The forms collect your name and email address, any company or phone details you choose to provide, and your message or free IT consultation request. Please do not submit passwords or confidential technical information.</p>
    <h2>Purpose and delivery</h2>
    <p>During this competition preview, the website administrator uses these details to respond to your inquiry and discuss the services or free IT consultation you request. Formspree is our external form-processing provider. It processes submissions for delivery to a temporary administrator-managed inbox and applies its spam protections. This is not an officially configured ITKeepers mailbox. Website acceptance confirms provider acceptance, not that an email has reached the inbox or been read.</p>
    <h2>Provider processing and retention</h2>
    <p>Formspree may store submissions and process technical information, such as IP address and browser details, to operate and protect its service. Formspree describes processing in the United States and other countries where it operates.</p>
    <p>How long Formspree makes submissions available depends on the account plan; its Privacy Policy describes additional retention for service, security and legal purposes. Copies delivered by email are retained separately in the temporary administrator-managed inbox. See <a class="disclosure-link" href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree's Privacy Policy</a> and its <a class="disclosure-link" href="https://formspree.io/plans/">submission archive information</a>.</p>
    <h2>Privacy questions and requests</h2>
    <p>For questions about your inquiry, or to request access, correction or deletion of information you submitted, use our <a class="disclosure-link" href="/contact/">contact form</a> and write 'Privacy request' in your message. Your request will be forwarded to the administrator managing inquiries for this competition preview.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
